From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolaos Karaolidis <nick@karaolidis.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:10:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fs: don't strip the same inode's cache over and over

After inode_lru_isolate() drops the page cache of an inode it returns
LRU_RETRY, and the walk restarts at the head of the list, where that
inode now is. If invalidate_mapping_pages() could not empty the mapping
(folios under writeback, locked or otherwise referenced), the inode is
stripped again until nr_to_walk runs out.

Before commit 2a0629834cd8 ("vfs: Don't evict inode under the inode lru
traversing context") the final iput() set I_REFERENCED, so the
restarted walk rotated the inode. Set I_REFERENCED when the mapping is
still populated after invalidation.

Only CONFIG_HIGHMEM kernels keep inodes with page cache on the inode
LRU, so only they are affected.

Fixes: 2a0629834cd8 ("vfs: Don't evict inode under the inode lru traversing context")
---
 fs/inode.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/inode.c b/fs/inode.c
index 8946e88af62d..2a455af72aa4 100644
--- a/fs/inode.c
+++ b/fs/inode.c
@@ -593,12 +593,11 @@ static void inode_pin_lru_isolating(struct inode *inode)
 
 static void inode_unpin_lru_isolating(struct inode *inode)
 {
-	spin_lock(&inode->i_lock);
+	lockdep_assert_held(&inode->i_lock);
 	WARN_ON(!(inode_state_read(inode) & I_LRU_ISOLATING));
 	inode_state_clear(inode, I_LRU_ISOLATING);
 	/* Called with inode->i_lock which ensures memory ordering. */
 	inode_wake_up_bit(inode, __I_LRU_ISOLATING);
-	spin_unlock(&inode->i_lock);
 }
 
 static void inode_wait_for_lru_isolating(struct inode *inode)
@@ -991,7 +990,13 @@ static enum lru_status inode_lru_isolate(struct list_head *item,
 		else
 			__count_vm_events(PGINODESTEAL, reap);
 		mm_account_reclaimed_pages(reap);
+
+		spin_lock(&inode->i_lock);
+		/* The walk restarts here: don't retry leftovers right away */
+		if (!mapping_empty(&inode->i_data))
+			inode_state_set(inode, I_REFERENCED);
 		inode_unpin_lru_isolating(inode);
+		spin_unlock(&inode->i_lock);
 		return LRU_RETRY;
 	}
 
